WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.320
This is another dimension, because the handgun
is concealable.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.060
It's a different conversation than just making
rifles.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.700
All handguns will eventually be available
for people to produce for themselves

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.760
in the privacy of their own homes.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.620
Gun control can never die, because it lives
in the hearts of men.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.900
No, gun control is not dead, it's undead.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.320
Gun control is undead.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.300
And uh-

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.820
we just keep killing it.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.640
But it just keeps coming back.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:38.500
In 2012 a then-25 year old crypto-anarchist
named Cody Wilson started Defense Distributed,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.840
an organization devoted to removing the barriers
from making firearms at home.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.520
The following year, defense distributed released
the Liberator

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.060
the first 3D printed pistol.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.560
The Liberator is a simple, single shot 380
caliber handgun.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.540
At the time, the replaceable barrels were
only considered safe for one shot.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.340
5 years after the Liberator debut, the technological
limitations of home made firearms

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.440
have started disappearing.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.780
The materials are cheaper and better, the
machines are more precise

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:12.510
and the software is more advanced.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:17.230
It's a new reality that hasn't entirely filtered
into public debates over gun control.

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:22.740
It outstrips people's daily experience, they
don't really understand what's taking place.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.000
This is a ghost gun .

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.800
Because now it is very easy and completely
legal to make a firearm

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.080
in the comfort of your own home.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.020
The era in which the government can even hope
to keep a fully functional firearm

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.760
out of the hands of someone truly determined
to get one is coming to an end.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:43.340
Now I can ship gun machines that help you
crank out 1911s in your kitchen all day long

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.200
and no one has anything to say about it.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.920
Because what is there to say about it?

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.820
By late 2014 Defense Distributed had raised
enough capital

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.520
to begin manufacturing the Ghost Gunner.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.920
A small machine that uses pre coded commands

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.080
to remove metal from unfinished firearm parts.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.420
Parts that when sold by a manufacturer

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.460
are legally required to contain a serial number.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.120
What comes out of the Ghost Gunner is a key
component of an untraceable

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.879
yet fully functional metal firearm.

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:16.390
In late 2017 Defense Distributed released
files that allow the ghost gunner

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.870
to mill out unfinished metal handgun frames.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:23.030
Wilson says the new focus on handguns is an
important step

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.140
towards the mainstreaming of home gun manufacturing.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.680
A lot of people living in an urban setting
like DC

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.640
wouldn't consider slinging an AR15 on their
back walking around the street.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.739
But they would at least think about whether
they wanted to have a handgun

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.700
concealed and made without anyone else's knowledge.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.739
While a 3D printer assembles objects out of
layers of plastic or other materials

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.140
a milling machine like the Ghost Gunner does
the opposite.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.400
Carving a solid piece of material based on
specifications spelled out in code.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.859
Defense Distributed sells the machine for
just under 1700 dollars.

00:02:56.859 --> 00:03:00.560
You can make a 1911 in your kitchen, make
it in your bath tub if you want

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.310
and no one has to know about it.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:07.189
It's really cool and it wasn't true last year
in the way that it's true now.

00:03:07.189 --> 00:03:10.749
Thanks to the internet, the newest generation
of homemade gun designs

00:03:10.749 --> 00:03:13.560
are approaching the quality of store bought
firearms.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:24.760
My name's Darren Booth I'm a union carpenter

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.460
start getting into 3D printing about 2014

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:33.019
and I was downloading different objects from
the internet, printing them out,

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.460
and I wasn't really satisfied with the way
they turned out.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.280
So I started getting into 3D design.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.940
And then that's when I heard about the Liberator.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.680
I like the Liberator, it's fine, you know
it's only good for one shot

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.340
so I thought, well, what can I do to make
it a little better?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.440
This is the latest version, the Shuty AP9.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.799
I make them out of PLA plastic but they hold
up well.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:03.159
This very gun here has probably had over 5000
rounds shot through it.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.500
The digital files that are used to create
guns using milling machines and 3D printers

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.260
are written and shared online by hobbyist
gun printers.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:15.129
Booth is a regular of the Fosscad group and
the community worked together

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:17.680
to make the digital files for the Shuty.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.120
But it's an open community, it's an open chat,
anybody can go on there

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.920
and just ask questions.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.070
I watched some of these groups begin like
on my own websites

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.419
when I used to host forums and IRC channels
and things like that.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:34.020
And it's great like in our earliest days I
imagined that.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.340
That would be what victory looked like.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.169
There would have to be communities taking
up these projects on their own.

00:04:38.169 --> 00:04:42.000
It's an intellectual exercise, it helps you,
you know and just it's fun

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.840
to come up with new ideas and exchange information.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.940
And this information exchange is at the core
of the home manufactured gun movement.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.740
The 3D printed gun was never itself.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.931
What we developed, what we shared online was
not the gun

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.680
but it was the files that could create the
gun.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.039
It's freeware for anybody that wants to build
it

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.580
hopefully somebody will make it even better.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.180
The Shuty requires additional parts made by
third parties

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.120
but those components can be freely ordered
on the internet

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.100
from unregulated vendors.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.280
Shoot a little low, a little low and to the
left.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:25.020
When the only thing you need to create a gun
at home is a tiny digital file

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.080
and a trip to the hardware store,

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.880
gun control becomes impractical.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:35.300
It may also be impossible to outlaw the distribution
of digital files used for handgun production.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.740
Wilson argues that an individual's right to
create and distribute blueprints for a gun

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:41.700
is protected by the First Amendment.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.000
Sharing that software was a political speech
act

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.880
and the software itself, because it can be
changed and evaluated

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.840
and understood by humans, the software itself
is speech.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.660
So it's about fighting about that information

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.040
not about what the information can become.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.819
In 2013 the State Department forced Defense
Distributed

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:03.280
to remove the download links to the files
for the Liberator,

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.540
claiming they violated the International Traffic
in Arms regulations or ITAR.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.259
They saw these kids you know online like

00:06:10.259 --> 00:06:14.039
'hey not only no gun control but we're gonna
destroy the whole concept

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:15.699
because the internet's gonna serve guns.'

00:06:15.699 --> 00:06:19.020
They were looking for a way to put their own
power over what we're doing.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:23.520
And the closest thing they could come up with
at the time was the ITAR.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.919
The ITAR is a set of regulations that govern
what kind of military materials

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.759
can leave the US and go to other countries.

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:33.129
The State Department and Justice Department
say

00:06:33.129 --> 00:06:37.129
sharing this type of information, gun files,
with American citizens on the internet

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:39.660
is tantamount to exporting it to foreigners.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:44.200
And this somehow violates a foreign affairs
power of the executive.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:49.200
Joined by the Second Amendment Foundation
and the prominent attorney Alan Gura,

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.020
Wilson challenged the State Department's order.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:56.660
In the spring of 2017 they petitioned the
Supreme Court for a temporary injunction

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.960
that would null the take down order until
their lawsuit was resolved.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:05.030
In January of 2018 the high court declined
to hear the case

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:09.020
sending it back to a lower court in Texas
to be argued on the merits.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:13.080
Yeah we're gonna win our case and it doesn't
meant that we have to win it in court

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.300
but, you know, we'll win in the court of public
opinion.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.120
And that doesn't mean that public opinion
will agree with us.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:26.199
In other words, the tools to build your own
firearms are already in circulation

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:31.100
but Wilson is trying to win legal protections
for future innovations in the space.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.320
Defense Distributed's focus on handguns is,
in part,

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:40.289
a legal strategy based on the 2008 Supreme
Court case District of Columbia versus Heller

00:07:40.289 --> 00:07:43.590
that affirmed the right to own a handgun for
self defense.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:48.240
The handgun is at the center of what is protected
in the Heller decision

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.860
as everything's understood now.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.210
So whereas AR15s may not ever be backed up
by the Supreme Court

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.259
there's no way of getting around, right now,

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.580
the protections that the Supreme Court gave
to the handgun.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:03.160
And so this is the core of the Second Amendment
liberty as it's currently understood.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:08.419
Now deploy-able, downloadable, manipulable,
you can do it in your garage.

00:08:08.419 --> 00:08:12.710
And so it's a kind of temptation, it's an
invitation to discourse if you will.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:17.259
Automated, off the books firearm technology
is a reality

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.600
and there's nothing anyone can do to change
that.

